    body: "Navi Pillay, a former International Criminal Court judge and United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, has won the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize.\n\nIn a statement announcing the award, the Nobel Committee praised Pillay's \"efforts to promote peace and international law\".\n\nBBC correspondent Joe Inwood explains how Pillay's childhood in South Africa led her to become a driving force in international law and human rights, from Rwanda to Gaza.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- United NationsUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Nobel PrizeUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
